# Does the Robe of Eyes grant the infravision its own page promises? Read by
# tools/check_robe_eyes.sh, bead inc-tek.8.8, finding PA-08-F12.
#
# The robe's Desc says it "grants the wearer 60 feet of Infravison"
# (lib/m_items.irh, entity AI_WONDER Effect "Robe of Eyes"). The entity's grant
# blocks gave Spot, Search, See Invisible, Improved Initiative and a gaze-attack
# handler, and no infravision at all.
#
# The oracle is the character dump, not a screen. [W]rite Dump on the character
# sheet calls TextTerm::DumpCharacter (src/Sheet.cpp), which writes the whole
# sheet to logs/<name>.txt. The "Special Abilities" block of that file prints
# "Infravision (%d ft)" from src/Sheet.cpp:538, and the number is
# Creature::AbilityLevel(CA_INFRAVISION) * 10. That function ADDS every
# EXTRA_ABILITY stati to the racial level (src/Creature.cpp:2983-2991), so a
# worn robe must raise the number rather than replace it.
#
# The character is the standard orc barbarian of chargen.keys. An orc already
# has 60 feet of its own (lib/races.irh, ABILITY(CA_INFRAVISION,6)), so the
# reading is 60 ft without the robe and must be 120 ft with it. A race with no
# infravision would read 0 and print no line at all, which is a weaker oracle:
# a missing line cannot tell "no grant" apart from "no section".
#
#   d W b e f o r e ENTER    dump the sheet before the robe exists. This is the
#                            baseline the two later dumps are measured against.
#   w y                      enter wizard mode and open its menu.
#   Item Acquisition         RIGHT*39 walks the glyph row to Wonderous Items:
#   RIGHT*39                 ItemGlyphs (src/Tables.cpp:320-365) puts
#                            -AI_WONDER 39 steps along, and the header line
#                            names the category.
#   @until "Robe of Eyes"    the candidate list has no menu letters, so the
#     DOWN                   cursor is walked. Three rows show and the MIDDLE
#                            one is selected, so the run stops on the pass where
#                            the wanted row first appears BELOW the cursor. One
#                            more DOWN selects it. The check does not trust that
#                            reasoning: it reads the robe's name back off the
#                            equipment screen.
#   i i SPACE d              open the inventory manager, select the Clothing
#                            slot, swap the robe into it, and drop the loincloth
#                            the swap lifted into the air. The manager will not
#                            close with anything in the air.
#   d W w o r n ENTER        the second dump. This is the reading under test:
#                            it must say 120 ft, not 60 ft.
#   i i SPACE d              and the robe back off, onto the floor.
#   d W o f f ENTER          the third dump. It must be back to 60 ft, because a
#                            bonus that outlives the item is worse than one that
#                            never arrives.

@include chargen.keys

d
@expect "Race   Orc"
W
b e f o r e ENTER
ESC

w
y
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*39
@until "Robe of Eyes" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER

i
i
SPACE
d
@dump:robe-worn
ESC
d
W
w o r n ENTER
ESC

i
i
SPACE
d
@dump:robe-removed
ESC
d
W
o f f ENTER
ESC
